[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":287},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news:\u002Fnews\u002F2007-07-29-1-6-2-beta1-i686-iso-released":3,"news-timeline":64},{"id":4,"title":5,"author":6,"body":7,"date":54,"description":55,"extension":56,"meta":57,"navigation":58,"path":59,"readingTime":60,"seo":61,"stem":62,"__hash__":63},"news\u002Fnews\u002F2007-07-29-1-6-2-beta1-i686-iso-released.md","1.6.2-beta1 (i686) ISO Released","sofar",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":50},"minimark",[10,14,17,20,28,31],[11,12,13],"p",{},"Hi,",[11,15,16],{},"We're happy to announce the first beta release of a new series of lunar-linux installer ISO's. Our new ISO's will be as easy to install as 1.6.1, but pack an extra punch: This series of ISO's preinstalls a basic Xfce4-4.4.1 desktop with XOrg-7.2, together with firefox, Thunderbird, pidgin, audacious, gimp and a few other basic desktop utilities.",[11,18,19],{},"We hope to make it easy for everyone to both enjoy playing and learning from a true source distro environment and both be productive quickly. The extra applications will give new users a fast start and should install easily on most (even brand new) hardware with the 2.6.22.1 kernel, but also give the user a welcome feeling on a freshly installed lunar-linux system.",[11,21,22,23,27],{},"At 585MB, this is a remarkable ISO that provides a great desktop installation to start with. I myself enjoyed testing this ISO on new systems, where even the wireless and 3D (open source radeon driver) worked without any other user interaction except for the command ",[24,25,26],"code",{},"startxfce4",". Hopefully you are as lucky on your hardware ;)",[11,29,30],{},"download it here:",[32,33,34,38,41,44,47],"ul",{},[35,36,37],"li",{},"Mirror",[35,39,40],{},"lunar-1.6.2-beta1-i686.iso.bz2 [HTTP]",[35,42,43],{},"MD5sums",[35,45,46],{},"lunar-1.6.2-beta1-i686.iso.bz2.md5",[35,48,49],{},"lunar-1.6.2-beta1-i686.iso.md5",{"title":51,"searchDepth":52,"depth":52,"links":53},"",3,[],"2007-07-29","The 1.6.2 beta installs a basic X